#
# generated/generation.json is the record of the last Generate. It holds a hash of the whole
# design, so when two people each ran Generate on their own branch it conflicts at every
# merge, whatever else they changed. Git treats it as a binary file: it writes no conflict
# markers into it (the file stays valid JSON) and keeps the version of the branch you are
# on. After the merge run:  harness-design-studio merge-fix PROJECT_FOLDER
# Every other file of the project is text and merges line by line.
generated/generation.json merge=binary linguist-generated=true
